4263fa65bcc74e80683f3fcd7ded47a83","file":"preprints/Rational-homology-and-Quillens-conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":15,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"5c120717deebd74179caf01ce013885c0b000f3f5eb6ed94670d05714b89df7c","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Rational-homology-and-Quillens-conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:7607d0209974bd7fa99b35573fc6fc34263fa65bcc74e80683f3fcd7ded47a83","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Rational-homology-and-Quillens-conjecture-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L15"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every finite group $G$ and every prime $p$, if $\\Op(G)=1$, then\n\\[\n\\widetilde H_*(\\Ap(G);\\Q)\\ne0.\n\\]\nHere reduced homology is augmented, so that the empty poset has\n$\\widetilde H_{-1}(\\varnothing;\\Q)=\\Q$."}
